{"name":"Golden Glow","hex":"#f9d77e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden glow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant, Rudbeckia laciniata"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_glow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rudbeckia laciniata","blocks":[{"text":"Rudbeckia laciniata, the cutleaf coneflower, is a species of flowering plant in the family Asteraceae. Other common names include cutleaf, goldenglow, green-headed coneflower, tall coneflower, sochan and thimbleweed. It is native to North American floodplains, stream banks, and moist forests. Although toxic to animals, the leaves have culinary uses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Oohangousou.JPG/330px-Oohangousou.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudbeckia_laciniata","wikidata":"Q1194614"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Oohangousou.JPG/500px-Oohangousou.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Oohangousou.JPG/500px-Oohangousou.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOohangousou.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Korina_2010-08-23_Rudbeckia_laciniata.jpg/500px-Korina_2010-08-23_Rudbeckia_laciniata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe